CONTROL STATEMENTS
Control statements is divided into 3 types:
-> Conditional Statements
-> Looping Statements
-> Jumping Statements

CONDITIONAL STATEMENTS
-> if
-> ifelse
-> elseif ladder
-> Nested if
-> switch

LOOPING STATEMENTS
-> for
-> while
-> dowhile

JUMPING STATEMENTS
-> continue
-> break
-> return

CONDITIONAL STATEMENTS 
SYNTAX - Set of rules & regulations used to write the code in correct manner.
IF Syntax:
  if condition{
    //block of code
}

Program
import java.util.Scanner;
class If
{
    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter a number: ");
        int a=sc.nextInt();
        int b=sc.nextInt();
        if(a<=b)
        {
            System.out.print("Condition is true");
        }
    }
}

IFELSE SYNTAX:
if condition{
    //block of code
}
else{
//block of code
}

Program
import java.util.Scanner;
class Ifelse
{
    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter a number: ");
        int a=sc.nextInt();
        int b=sc.nextInt();
        if(a<=b)
        {
            System.out.print("Condition is true");
        }
        else
        {
            System.out.print("Condition is false");
        }
    }
}


